<title>CANADA: CBRS reinstates Southam debt ratings.</title>
<headline>CBRS reinstates Southam debt ratings.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Bond Rating Service said on Thursday it reinstated its ratings on Southam Inc's debt with a stable outlook following Hollinger Inc's failed bid for the company.</p>
<p>CBRS said it reinstated ratings of A-2 (high) on Southam's commercial paper and and B++ (high) on the publisher's medium-term notes.</p>
<p>Hollinger had offered Southam minority shareholders C$23.50 per share for the 49.55 percent of stock it did not already own, but less than 17 percent of the shares were tendered to the bid.</p>
<p>The newly acquired shares brought Hollinger's ownership interest in Southam to 58.6 percent. ((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
